# `Cargo.lock` is COMMITTED, not ignored.
#
# The advice to ignore it applies to published libraries, and even there Cargo's
# own guidance now recommends committing: a lock is simply ignored when the
# package is consumed as a dependency, so there is no downside. This repo ships
# 22 binaries, which is the unambiguous commit case.
#
# Concretely, ignoring it meant CI re-resolved every dependency on every run.
# `libgit2-sys 0.18.7` shipped a PCRE1 -> PCRE2 swap with unprefixed symbols and
# broke the Windows builds of `sniff`, `darkmatter`, and `tree-hugger` on an
# upstream release day, with no local change and nothing in the repo recording
# which version had been in play. A past CI run could not be reproduced.
#
# One lock per workspace root or excluded package. A lock inside a workspace
# MEMBER is a stray artifact Cargo never consults — `research/{lib,cli}` each had
# one, four months stale, from before they joined the workspace.

# Insta pending snapshots (transient — should never be committed)
**/*.snap.new
**/*.pending-snap

.opencode/package-lock.json
# Timing artifacts emitted by `just _lint` / `just _test` recipes
**/lint-*-timing.jsonl
**/test-*-timing.jsonl

**/lint-*timing.jsonl
**/test-*timing.jsonl
.claudine/tmp/
**/tmp-stream*
# do not add gitnexus cache
.gitnexus/*

/.claude/settings.local.json
/.system-prompt.md
.codex/config.toml

# Python bytecode from scripts/ci test runs
__pycache__/
*.pyc
